{
  "headline": "FDA's records show no shortage signal for the WG Critical Care product at our plants; Merck Sharp & Dohme listings are marked To Be Discontinued with initial postings 2026-01-08 and 2026-09-09",
  "headline_cites": ["E4", "E5", "E6"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "The imipenem and cilastatin vials used at Corvale East, Corvale General, and Corvale Lakeside all carry NDC 44567-705-10 and SPL set ID 46f54df9-5afe-430c-aa19-0d84c2044b0b, identifying the labeler as WG Critical Care, LLC and the manufacturing plant as Zambon Switzerland Ltd. in Cadempino.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E2", "E3", "E4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA's shortage list contains two Merck Sharp & Dohme entries for imipenem-containing products, both status To Be Discontinued, with initial posting dates 2026-01-08 and 2026-09-09, but neither references the WG Critical Care NDC or the Zambon plant.",
      "cites": ["E5", "E6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the FDA has not posted a shortage signal for the WG Critical Care product manufactured at Zambon Switzerland, the current supply pressure at Corvale East reflects local demand rather than a federally tracked shortage.",
      "cites": ["E4", "E5", "E6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 66 units at 16.5 per day, giving 4 days on hand, while Corvale Lakeside holds 105 units at 3.5 per day, giving 30 days on hand and enough surplus to transfer 55 units and still retain two weeks of supply.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Transferring 55 units from Corvale Lakeside to Corvale East would raise Corvale East to approximately 7 days on hand and leave Corvale Lakeside with roughly 14 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D3"]
    }
  ]
}
